WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.040
( Theme music playing )

2
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.000
-( people shouting )
-( swords clanging )

3
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.320
-( dogs barking )
-( ravens cawing )

4
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.320
-( banging )
-( gasps )

5
00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.480
( caws )

6
00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.320
I've taken your castle.

7
00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.040
-Theon?
-It's prince Theon now.

8
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.800
Get up. You have to get dressed.
I've taken Winterfell.

9
00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.760
I took it. I'm occupying it.

10
00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:45.800
I sent men over the walls
With grappling claws and ropes.

11
00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.760
-Why?
-To take the castle.

12
00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:53.000
-You went with Robb.
-And he sent me back to Pyke.

13
00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.400
I'm a Greyjoy. I can't fight for Robb
And my father both.

14
00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.400
-Where's hodor?
-I don't know.

15
00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.760
Find the halfwit.

16
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:05.560
My men are bringing your people
Together in the courtyard.

17
00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.040
Why?

18
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.000
So you and I can
Go down and tell them

19
00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.680
-How you've yielded Winterfell to me.
-I won't.

20
00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.760
Yes. you will.

21
00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:16.760
I won't. I'll never yield.

22
00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.680
We'll fight you
And throw you out.

23
00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.720
( sighs )

24
00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:25.840
The castle is mine.

25
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.240
But these people are still yours.

26
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.240
You'll yield to keep them safe.

27
00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.680
To keep them alive.

28
00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.320
That's what a good lord would do.

29
00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.720
Think carefully about
What you want to say.

30
00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:45.600
Theon.

31
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:47.520
Did you hate us the whole time?

32
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.120
-( thunder rumbles )
-( horse whinnies )

33
00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:57.160
I've yielded Winterfell to Theon.

34
00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.040
Louder.

35
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:00.760
Say prince Theon.

36
00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.720
I've yielded Winterfell
To prince Theon.

37
00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.440
You all know me.

38
00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.000
Aye. we know you for
A steaming sack of shit.

39
00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.800
Farlen. you be silent.

40
00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.640
Listen to your little lord. farlen.

41
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.440
He has more sense than you do.

42
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:16.440
All of you should do as he commands.

43
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:20.000
My father has donned
The ancient crown of salt and rock

44
00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:23.360
And declared himself
King of the iron islands.

45
00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.440
He claims the north as well
By right of conquest.

46
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.200
You are all his subjects.

47
00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.920
Bugger that. I serve the Starks.

48
00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:34.240
-If you think you can
Hold the north with this...
-Shut up!

49
00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.560
Theon:
If you serve me as loyally
As you served Ned Stark.

50
00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:40.240
I will be as good to you
As he ever was.

51
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.360
Betray me. and you will
Wish you hadn't.

52
00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:44.160
( crowd murmuring )

53
00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.240
Maester Luwin. send a raven to Pyke

54
00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.920
Informing my father
Of my victory here

55
00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.280
And one to Deepwood Motte
To my sister.

56
00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.560
Inform her that she's
To bring 500 men to Winterfell.

57
00:04:56.720 --> 00:04:58.600
( crowd murmuring )

58
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.080
You are a maester of the citadel

59
00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.040
Sworn to serve the lord
Of Winterfell. are you not?

60
00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.520
I am.

61
00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.360
I am the lord of Winterfell

62
00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.040
As Bran just informed you.

63
00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.480
Send the ravens.

64
00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.560
My lord.

65
00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.360
My Lord Greyjoy.

66
00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:25.720
I see you've finally learned
How to address your betters.

67
00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.200
What do you want?

68
00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.520
I was brought here
A captive.

69
00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.760
You were here the day
I was taken.

70
00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.480
I'm the one who took you.
What of it?

71
00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.160
Let me serve you.

72
00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:40.640
Theon:
Serve me how?

73
00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:43.040
I need fighters. not kitchen sluts.

74
00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.080
It was Robb Stark who
Put me in the kitchens.

75
00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.520
Put a spear in my hand again.

76
00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:50.520
So you can bury it in my neck?

77
00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:53.400
Do you take me for a fool?
Get up.

78
00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:56.320
Step aside.

79
00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:58.680
Why?

80
00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:02.040
It's your dream. little lord.

81
00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:05.400
The ocean has come
To swallow this place.

82
00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.200
I ain't letting it drown me.

83
00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:10.640
-And in a few days' time...
-Rodrik: Greyjoy!

84
00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.720
Woman:
What have they done to him?

85
00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.640
We caught this one on his way back
From Torrhen's Square.

86
00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.520
Took out two of ours
Before I got his sword.

87
00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:26.920
Ser Rodrik. it grieves me that
We meet as foes.

88
00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:30.600
It grieves me you've less honor
Than a back alley whore.

89
00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:33.880
You were raised here under this roof.

90
00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.520
-These people are your people.
-They are not my people.

91
00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.600
King Robb thought of you
As a brother.

92
00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:41.440
My brothers are dead.

93
00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.160
They died fighting
Stark men. men like you.

94
00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:47.520
Aye. they died fighting
A war your father started.

95
00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:49.720
Lord Stark raised you
Among his own sons.

96
00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.800
Among them. but not one of them.

97
00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.520
I was his hostage taken from my home.

98
00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:56.080
If he were alive to see this...

99
00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.920
He's not. He's dead.

100
00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.880
The seven kingdoms are at war.

101
00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:02.200
And Winterfell is mine.

102
00:07:02.360 --> 00:07:04.720
I should have put
A sword in your belly

103
00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:06.280
Instead of in your hand.

104
00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.760
You've served this house
Faithfully. old man.

105
00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.240
But keep talking and I'll...

106
00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:13.040
( grunts )

107
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.840
Take him to the cells. Lock him up...

108
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.600
My prince.

109
00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.040
You cannot let that stand.
He must pay.

110
00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:21.960
I'll lock him in a cell
Until he rots...

111
00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:24.880
No. he has to pay the iron price.

112
00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.800
They'll never respect
You while he lives.

113
00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:41.560
( thunder rumbles )

114
00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.520
Ser Rodrik.

115
00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.040
I sentence you to death.

116
00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:51.400
No! You said no harm
Would come to them if I yielded.

117
00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:53.680
The old man couldn't
Keep his mouth shut.

118
00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:56.280
I urge you not to make
A hasty decision.

119
00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.040
He disrespected me

120
00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.600
In front of my men.
That was his decision. not mine.

121
00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:02.880
He is worth more
To you alive than dead.

122
00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.800
The Starks will pay.

123
00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.640
Please. Theon.

124
00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.320
Think what you do.

125
00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.520
You'll address me as prince Theon

126
00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.320
Or you'll be next.

127
00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.200
Come.

128
00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.760
No!

129
00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.720
-No!
-Bran: Theon!

130
00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.600
Please!

131
00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.440
Ser Rodrik!

132
00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.280
He who passes the sentence
Should swing the sword.

133
00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.640
-Bran: I'm begging you!
-Coward.

134
00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.520
Stop! Stop right now!

135
00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:49.320
You don't give commands anymore.
Little lord.

136
00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.720
-Please. stop this.
Please stop him.
-Rodrik: hush now. child.

137
00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.560
I'm off to see your father.

138
00:08:56.840 --> 00:08:59.600
Bran:
You said no harm would come!

139
00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.120
You said no harm would come.
Theon. please.

140
00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:04.960
Any last words. old man?

141
00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.680
Gods help you. Theon Greyjoy.

142
00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:09.800
Now you are truly lost.

143
00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.320
Bran:
Theon. please. don't.

144
00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:15.040
-Rickon: do something.
-Bran: I'll do anything. Please!

145
00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.800
Rickon:
No. please. stop it!

146
00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.720
-( grunts )
-( screams )

147
00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:30.440
-( Bran wailing )
-( thunder rumbling )

148
00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.320
( panting )

149
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.880
( wind howling )

150
00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.200
Jon:
Ghost. stay with us.

151
00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.200
Ghost!

152
00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.920
There goes your pet.

153
00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.560
Jon:
He's not a pet.

154
00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:56.760
Qhorin:
You're right. he's not.

155
00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.240
You can't tame a wild thing.

156
00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:01.080
You can't trust a wild thing.

157
00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.920
-Ghost is different.
-So you think.

158
00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:06.240
Wild creatures have their own rules.

159
00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.360
Their own reasons.

160
00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:10.280
And you'll never know them.

161
00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.840
Now the wildlings we're looking for

162
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
Sleep during the day
And hunt at night.

163
00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.000
I thought you said
You couldn't know wild things.

164
00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.000
I said you can't.

165
00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:25.880
They find a nice cave
To hide in while the sun's up

166
00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:27.680
And do their killing when it's dark.

167
00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:30.600
-We could do the same.
-No. we couldn't.

168
00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.760
This is their country.

169
00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.680
They know where to walk.
Where not to walk.

170
00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.560
I've lost good men
Who fell into a crevasse

171
00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.480
They didn't see till they were in it.

172
00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:43.080
My father always said
I'm of the north.

173
00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.880
( chuckles )

174
00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.600
-I wasn't joking.
-Look around. boy.

175
00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:50.760
This look like home to you?

176
00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.720
You start thinking
You know this place. it'll kill you.

177
00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.040
You understand me?

178
00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:59.400
No. you don't.

179
00:10:59.560 --> 00:11:01.320
We're at war.

180
00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:03.080
We've always been at war.

181
00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:05.440
It's never going to end
'Cause we're not fighting an enemy.

182
00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:08.880
We're fighting the north
And it's not going anywhere.

183
00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.800
The watch has given
You a great gift.

184
00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.240
You only have one thing
To give in return...

185
00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:17.000
-Your life.
-I'll gladly give my life.

186
00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.280
I don't want you
To be glad about it.

187
00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:21.240
I want you to curse and fight

188
00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:23.560
Until your heart's done pumping.

189
00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:26.000
And know this. boy...

190
00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:29.600
Your death will be a gift
For them south of the wall.

191
00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:31.720
They'll never know what you've done.

192
00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.240
They'll never know how you died.

193
00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.200
They won't even know your damn name.

194
00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.080
But they'll be alive because
Some nameless bastard

195
00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.520
North of the wall
Gave his life for theirs.

196
00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.520
Now. do you understand me?

197
00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:46.320
I do.

198
00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:48.400
You're even dumber than you look.

199
00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:51.760
It's just words. boy.

200
00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:53.680
To keep us a little
Warmer in the night.

201
00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:56.760
Make us feel like
We've got a purpose.

202
00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:59.240
( laughs )
Come on.

203
00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:02.680
We've got to find these goat fuckers
Before night falls and they find us.

204
00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.600
-Can you read?
-My lord?

205
00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:19.360
Can you read?

206
00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:25.480
This letter detailing
Our infantry movements

207
00:12:25.640 --> 00:12:28.000
Was meant for Lord Damon
Of house Marbrand.

208
00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:31.680
It was sent to Lord Marlyn
Of house Dormand.

209
00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:33.640
My apologies. my lord. I must have...

210
00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:37.000
Girl. fetch me
The "history of the greater
And the lesser houses."

211
00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:39.680
It's the one on the...
( chuckles )

212
00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:45.960
My cupbearer can read
Better than you.

213
00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:57.120
To whom does
House Dormand owe allegiance?

214
00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.640
My lord. I...

215
00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:04.360
To the Starks of Winterfell!

216
00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:08.200
Who have 20.000 men and my son!

217
00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:11.760
I judged you might be
Good for something more

218
00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:14.200
Than brutalizing peasants.

219
00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:16.360
I see I overestimated you.

220
00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:21.200
If you ever put my son's
Life at risk again. I'll...

221
00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.480
Leave us.

222
00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:35.240
Put the book away. girl.
( door opens )

223
00:13:35.400 --> 00:13:37.480
( door closes )

224
00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:42.760
Maybe you should devise
Our next battle plan while
You're about it.

225
00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:44.680
( knocking )

226
00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.200
( door opens )

227
00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.680
Lord Petyr Baelish.

228
00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:51.360
Mmm.

229
00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.480
Give us the room.

230
00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.560
Clear all this.

231
00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:08.120
-Lord Tywin.
-Baelish.

232
00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:18.640
-Wine?
-Thank you.

233
00:14:21.600 --> 00:14:23.320
What news from the capital?

234
00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:26.520
I traveled here directly
From Renly Baratheon's camp.

235
00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.720
Ah. the late King Renly.

236
00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.960
Rather a short reign.

237
00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.800
Murdered by a woman. I hear.

238
00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:34.720
So they say.

239
00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:39.640
There has been talk
Of other forces at work.

240
00:14:39.800 --> 00:14:42.040
Dark forces.

241
00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.320
Here.

242
00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.680
( scoffs )
Men love to blame demons

243
00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:52.200
When their grand plans unravel.

244
00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:54.880
It is my belief
That a moment of chaos

245
00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:57.400
Affords opportunities
Lost soon after.

246
00:14:57.560 --> 00:15:00.360
You say that as if you were
The first man alive to think it.

247
00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:03.360
Yes. a crisis is an opportunity.

248
00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:05.760
What other brilliant insights
Have you brought me today?

249
00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.400
After the Lannisters and the Starks.

250
00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.760
The tyrells command
The largest host.

251
00:15:09.920 --> 00:15:11.920
Their lands are the most
Fertile in the seven kingdoms.

252
00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:15.720
-feeding horses and soldiers.
-Yes. yes. yes.

253
00:15:15.880 --> 00:15:19.960
The tyrells have not yet declared
For any of the surviving kings.

254
00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:23.000
Loras wants revenge.
He blames Stannis for Renly's death.

255
00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:25.560
And Margaery...

256
00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:27.320
Wants to be queen.

257
00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.000
Yes. she does.

258
00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:35.000
House Tyrell rebelled
Against the iron throne.

259
00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.440
-against my grandson.
-They did.

260
00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.600
And perhaps that treason
Should be punished

261
00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.560
One day.

262
00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:46.360
After Stannis
And Robb Stark are defeated.

263
00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:50.560
More wine for Lord Baelish.

264
00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:59.760
If you will allow me to represent
Your family's interests.

265
00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.800
I believe that
An advantageous agreement...

266
00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:04.680
The Tyrell host has
Returned to Highgarden?

267
00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:06.840
They have.

268
00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.680
Pardon. my lord.

269
00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.560
It's only wine.

270
00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:13.920
You would ride there yourself?

271
00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.840
Tonight. with your leave.

272
00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.960
I'll have an answer by nightfall.

273
00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.520
That'll be all. girl.

274
00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:26.440
What else?

275
00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.520
On your son Tyrion's directive.

276
00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.920
I met with Catelyn Stark.

277
00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.520
Why?

278
00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:34.880
Littlefinger: he had
An interesting proposal for her

279
00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:37.800
-concerning her daughters.
-Hmm.

280
00:17:05.520 --> 00:17:07.400
-( groans )
-( shouting )

281
00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:28.080
-A girl.
-A wildling.

282
00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.520
-We could question her.
-You could.

283
00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.200
She won't answer.

284
00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:37.880
I've known a wildling to bite off
His tongue instead of talking.

285
00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:41.480
-What's your name?
-Ygritte.

286
00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:44.480
She was reaching for this ax
When you got to her.

287
00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:48.080
Give her half a chance.
She'll bury it in your face.

288
00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:50.640
I gave you my name.

289
00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.240
I'm Jon Snow.

290
00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.560
You ought to burn them you killed.

291
00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:05.040
Qhorin:
We'd need a big fire for that.

292
00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:08.960
Tell me. Ygritte.

293
00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:10.920
Why do you want us
To build a big fire?

294
00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:14.120
Are there some more
Friends in the area?

295
00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.280
Burn them or maybe you'll
Need those swords again.

296
00:18:17.440 --> 00:18:19.800
Our boy here's already
Killed one dead man.

297
00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:22.120
He can do it again if he has to.

298
00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.600
What waits beyond the pass?

299
00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:26.560
-The free folk.
-How many?

300
00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:28.400
( chuckles )

301
00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:30.360
Hundreds and thousands.

302
00:18:30.520 --> 00:18:32.720
More than you've ever seen. crow.

303
00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:36.040
Why come to the mountains?

304
00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:38.720
What's in the frostfangs
Your king could want?

305
00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:48.280
Do you mean to march on the wall?

306
00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.320
Do you know
Who I am. girl?

307
00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:58.760
Qhorin Halfhand.

308
00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:03.400
Tell me true.
If your people captured me.

309
00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:05.400
Would they take me prisoner?

310
00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:07.440
They'd take your head
Off your shoulders

311
00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.480
If they was feeling kind.

312
00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:12.000
If not. they'd kill you slow.

313
00:19:12.160 --> 00:19:14.520
( sighs )

314
00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:17.040
We have no food for her.

315
00:19:17.200 --> 00:19:19.160
Can't spare a man to watch her.

316
00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:22.240
Can't let her go. She'll bring
Mance Rayder's army down on us.

317
00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.200
It needs to be done.

318
00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:26.560
-Want me to do it?
-No.

319
00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.680
No. I'll do it.

320
00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.360
Come. brothers.

321
00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:34.480
We'll leave him to it.

322
00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:36.320
We'll meet you at the top.

323
00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:37.840
Don't take too long.

324
00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:39.320
We're deep in their country now.

325
00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:47.040
( bird screeches )

326
00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:55.360
You never killed
A woman before. did you?

327
00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:58.120
You don't need to do it.

328
00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:00.160
Mance would take you.
I know he would.

329
00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:03.080
There's secret ways.

330
00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.720
The crows would never catch us.

331
00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:08.560
I'm as much a crow as they are.

332
00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.000
Will you burn me...

333
00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:23.920
After?

334
00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:26.480
Can't.

335
00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:28.720
Someone might see the smoke.

336
00:20:34.280 --> 00:20:36.480
Strike hard and true.

337
00:20:36.640 --> 00:20:38.720
Jon Snow.

338
00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:40.880
Or I'll come back and haunt you.

339
00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:47.360
That's cold.

340
00:20:49.760 --> 00:20:51.120
Go on.

341
00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:53.000
Be quick about it.

342
00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:01.440
Do it.

343
00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:06.560
Bastard. do it!

344
00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:10.040
-( grunts )
-( clangs )

345
00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:17.480
( breathing heavily )

346
00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:19.400
( grunts )

347
00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:16.760
( grunts )

348
00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:19.120
( panting )

349
00:22:19.280 --> 00:22:21.960
You can't do it. We both know it.

350
00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:29.040
The sun's going down. Jon Snow.

351
00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:33.480
-And your friends are nowhere close.
-I'll find them.

352
00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:36.960
Call for them. Go on.

353
00:22:37.120 --> 00:22:38.640
Call loudly.

354
00:22:45.600 --> 00:22:47.840
Man:
May the seven guide
The princess on her journey.

355
00:22:48.000 --> 00:22:49.320
( crying )

356
00:22:49.480 --> 00:22:51.080
May the mother give her health.

357
00:22:51.240 --> 00:22:53.400
May the crone give her wisdom.

358
00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:56.440
May the warrior give her courage.

359
00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:58.880
-( crying )
-( septon continues )

360
00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:03.120
One day I pray you love someone.

361
00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:06.840
I pray you love her so much.

362
00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:08.960
When you close your eyes.
You see her face.

363
00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:13.800
I want that for you.

364
00:23:13.960 --> 00:23:17.200
I want you to know what
It's like to love someone.

365
00:23:17.360 --> 00:23:20.400
To truly love someone.

366
00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:22.600
Before I take her from you.

367
00:23:28.440 --> 00:23:31.320
( septon continues )

368
00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:37.040
( crying )

369
00:23:39.400 --> 00:23:42.080
You sound like a little cat
Mewling for his mother.

370
00:23:42.240 --> 00:23:43.560
Princes don't cry.

371
00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:46.320
-I saw you cry.
-Did you say something. my lady?

372
00:23:46.480 --> 00:23:49.480
My little brother cried
When I left Winterfell.

373
00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:52.720
-So?
-It seems a normal thing.

374
00:23:52.880 --> 00:23:54.600
Is your little brother a prince?

375
00:23:54.760 --> 00:23:56.720
No.

376
00:23:56.880 --> 00:23:58.800
Not really relevant. then. is it?

377
00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:04.440
Come. dog.

378
00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:13.840
Man:
Hail. Joffrey!

379
00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.080
-Hail to the king.
-( man laughs )

380
00:24:18.320 --> 00:24:19.680
Seven blessings on you.
Your grace.

381
00:24:19.840 --> 00:24:21.960
Man:
Murderer! Bastard!

382
00:24:22.120 --> 00:24:23.440
All hail the king.

383
00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:25.600
Man:
He's no king. He's a bastard!

384
00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:27.200
( people laughing )

385
00:24:27.360 --> 00:24:28.920
Please. your grace. we're hungry.

386
00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:31.640
( crowd shouting )

387
00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:34.600
-Man: freak!
-Get the prince back to the keep now.

388
00:24:34.760 --> 00:24:37.000
Yes. my lord. Come. quickly.

389
00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:39.000
Woman: please. your grace.
Give us some food!

390
00:24:39.160 --> 00:24:41.360
Man:
Bread. your grace. please!

391
00:24:42.920 --> 00:24:44.280
-( groans )
-( crowd gasps )

392
00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:46.120
Who threw that?

393
00:24:46.280 --> 00:24:47.960
I want the man
Who threw that.

394
00:24:48.120 --> 00:24:49.880
-Find who did that
And bring him to me!
-Man: hold on!

395
00:24:50.040 --> 00:24:53.320
-Hold them back!
-Joffrey: just kill them!
Kill them all!

396
00:24:59.200 --> 00:25:01.360
-Move. Move!
-Man: pull back!

397
00:25:01.520 --> 00:25:03.240
Man:
Tear him to pieces!

398
00:25:03.400 --> 00:25:06.080
What are you doing?
I want these people executed!

399
00:25:06.240 --> 00:25:08.160
And they want the same for you.

400
00:25:20.920 --> 00:25:23.000
( septon screaming )

401
00:25:29.800 --> 00:25:32.320
( cheering )

402
00:25:33.520 --> 00:25:35.920
Where's Sansa?

403
00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:38.920
-( screaming )
-Man: through the door!

404
00:25:39.080 --> 00:25:40.720
-( Growls )
-Man #2: come on!

405
00:25:40.880 --> 00:25:42.640
( shouting )

406
00:25:45.120 --> 00:25:47.280
-( whimpering )
-Protect the king!

407
00:25:47.440 --> 00:25:49.880
-Get back!
-Fall back!

408
00:25:50.040 --> 00:25:51.880
-Move!
-To the gates!

409
00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:06.680
-Come in! Come in!
-Keep him safe!

410
00:26:06.840 --> 00:26:09.080
-( crowd shouting )
-People: motherfucker!

411
00:26:09.240 --> 00:26:11.880
-Watch out. Hold them back.
-Come on.

412
00:26:15.400 --> 00:26:17.080
( whimpers )

413
00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:21.160
-Hey!
-( laughs )

414
00:26:21.320 --> 00:26:22.920
Traitors!

415
00:26:23.080 --> 00:26:24.760
I'll have all their heads.

416
00:26:24.920 --> 00:26:26.480
Oh. you blind. bloody fool.

417
00:26:26.640 --> 00:26:28.400
You can't insult me.

418
00:26:28.560 --> 00:26:31.280
We've had vicious kings
And we've had idiot kings.

419
00:26:31.440 --> 00:26:34.000
But I don't know if
We've ever been cursed with
A vicious idiot for a king.

420
00:26:34.160 --> 00:26:35.720
-You can't...
-I can. I am.

421
00:26:35.880 --> 00:26:37.280
They attacked me!

422
00:26:37.440 --> 00:26:40.640
They threw a cow pie at you.
So you decided to kill them all?

423
00:26:40.800 --> 00:26:42.360
They're starving. you fool.

424
00:26:42.520 --> 00:26:44.080
All because of a war you started.

425
00:26:44.240 --> 00:26:46.480
You're talking to a king!
( shrieks )

426
00:26:46.640 --> 00:26:48.760
And now I've struck a king.

427
00:26:48.920 --> 00:26:50.800
Did my hand fall from my wrist?

428
00:26:50.960 --> 00:26:52.720
Where is the Stark girl?

429
00:26:52.880 --> 00:26:54.320
Let them have her.

430
00:26:54.480 --> 00:26:57.600
If she dies. you'll never
Get your uncle Jaime back.

431
00:26:57.760 --> 00:27:00.320
You owe him quite a bit. you know.

432
00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:03.840
( panting )

433
00:27:08.640 --> 00:27:10.440
-Where are you going?
-( cloth rips )

434
00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:13.920
-( laughing )
-You ever been fucked. little girl?

435
00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:17.160
-( whimpering )
-Come here.

436
00:27:17.320 --> 00:27:19.160
Take some men
And go and find the Stark girl.

437
00:27:19.320 --> 00:27:20.800
I take my orders from the king.

438
00:27:22.600 --> 00:27:24.560
Man:
This way!

439
00:27:24.720 --> 00:27:27.040
( screaming )

440
00:27:29.880 --> 00:27:32.320
( sobbing )
Please!

441
00:27:32.480 --> 00:27:33.920
No. no.

442
00:27:37.280 --> 00:27:39.320
( screams )

443
00:27:41.320 --> 00:27:42.680
( choking )

444
00:27:42.840 --> 00:27:44.520
( grunts )

445
00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:50.080
( grunts )

446
00:27:50.240 --> 00:27:52.400
( Sansa breathing heavily )

447
00:27:52.560 --> 00:27:54.560
Please!

448
00:27:56.360 --> 00:27:58.440
You're all right now. little bird.

449
00:27:58.600 --> 00:28:00.360
You're all right.

450
00:28:03.880 --> 00:28:05.640
( crowd shouting )

451
00:28:05.800 --> 00:28:07.400
( screams )

452
00:28:13.600 --> 00:28:17.080
-Man: we'll get you. We'll get you.
-Man #2: this way.

453
00:28:19.280 --> 00:28:22.200
-Are you hurt. my lady?
-The little bird's bleeding.

454
00:28:22.360 --> 00:28:23.840
Someone take her back to her cage.

455
00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:25.600
See to that cut.

456
00:28:25.760 --> 00:28:30.000
-Well done. Clegane.
-I didn't do it for you.

457
00:28:32.080 --> 00:28:33.800
He shouldn't make me wait.

458
00:28:33.960 --> 00:28:37.920
The spice king is
The second wealthiest man in Qarth.

459
00:28:38.080 --> 00:28:40.000
He makes everyone wait.

460
00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:43.200
Of course. you could have
Avoided this embarrassment

461
00:28:43.360 --> 00:28:45.600
If you married
The wealthiest man in Qarth.

462
00:28:45.760 --> 00:28:47.600
I already have a husband.

463
00:28:47.760 --> 00:28:49.880
Khal Drogo is gone. khaleesi.

464
00:28:50.040 --> 00:28:53.520
You are far too young
To be a widow forever

465
00:28:53.680 --> 00:28:55.760
And far too beautiful.

466
00:28:55.920 --> 00:28:57.560
And you are far too smart

467
00:28:57.720 --> 00:29:00.880
To think that I will
Succumb to flattery.

468
00:29:01.040 --> 00:29:02.800
I have traveled
Very far in my life

469
00:29:02.960 --> 00:29:04.520
And met many women.

470
00:29:04.680 --> 00:29:06.440
But none that are
Immune to flattery.

471
00:29:06.600 --> 00:29:09.320
-The mother of dragons!
-Ah.

472
00:29:09.480 --> 00:29:10.840
Here he comes.

473
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:14.280
Forgive me.
I had terrible dreams last night.

474
00:29:14.440 --> 00:29:15.920
Terrible dreams.

475
00:29:16.080 --> 00:29:18.880
I could not sleep
Until the sun was shining

476
00:29:19.040 --> 00:29:21.360
And the birds were singing.

477
00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:24.120
Look what a beauty you are

478
00:29:24.280 --> 00:29:26.520
Now the red waste
Has been washed off you.

479
00:29:26.680 --> 00:29:29.800
I am sorry about
All that unpleasantness.

480
00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:33.880
The silver hair of a true Targaryen.

481
00:29:34.040 --> 00:29:37.520
Xaro Xhoan Daxos.
She is far too lovely

482
00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:39.920
For a glorified
Dockworker like yourself.

483
00:29:40.080 --> 00:29:43.320
Very true. and yet they say
That your grandfather.

484
00:29:43.480 --> 00:29:45.360
Who sold pepper
Off the back of a wagon.

485
00:29:45.520 --> 00:29:48.640
Married a lady far lovelier
And higher born than himself.

486
00:29:48.800 --> 00:29:50.880
Every lady alive was lovelier

487
00:29:51.040 --> 00:29:53.120
And higher born than my grandfather.

488
00:29:53.280 --> 00:29:54.720
-( laughs )
-Daenerys: ahem.

489
00:29:54.880 --> 00:29:58.280
Did my servants not offer you
Something to eat. to drink?

490
00:29:58.440 --> 00:30:00.080
I'll have them flogged
In the square.

491
00:30:00.240 --> 00:30:01.920
Thank you. my lord.
You are a gracious host.

492
00:30:02.080 --> 00:30:04.800
But there is no servant alive
That can bring me what I want.

493
00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:07.520
Oh. she has a talent
For drama. this one.

494
00:30:07.680 --> 00:30:11.480
So. my little princess.
What is it you want?

495
00:30:11.640 --> 00:30:13.000
My birthright...

496
00:30:13.160 --> 00:30:14.760
The seven kingdoms of Westeros.

497
00:30:14.920 --> 00:30:17.440
I fear I'm no better than
A servant in this regard.

498
00:30:17.600 --> 00:30:19.360
I cannot give you what I do not have.

499
00:30:19.520 --> 00:30:21.960
I'm not asking you for the kingdoms.

500
00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:25.080
I'm asking you for ships.
I need to cross the narrow sea.

501
00:30:25.240 --> 00:30:28.480
I need my ships as well.
I use them. you see.

502
00:30:28.640 --> 00:30:30.800
To bring spices from
One port to another.

503
00:30:30.960 --> 00:30:32.440
Whatever you grant me
Now will be repaid

504
00:30:32.600 --> 00:30:34.960
Three times over when
I retake the iron throne.

505
00:30:35.120 --> 00:30:36.920
Retake?

506
00:30:37.080 --> 00:30:38.520
Did you once sit on the iron throne?

507
00:30:38.680 --> 00:30:41.280
My father sat there
Before he was murdered.

508
00:30:41.440 --> 00:30:43.600
But if you did not
Sit on it yourself.

509
00:30:43.760 --> 00:30:47.000
Would it not be correct
To say take the iron throne?

510
00:30:47.160 --> 00:30:48.920
I didn't come here to argue grammar.

511
00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:51.640
Of course not.
You came to take my ships.

512
00:30:51.800 --> 00:30:54.200
So let me explain my position.

513
00:30:54.360 --> 00:30:56.160
Little princess.

514
00:30:56.320 --> 00:30:59.360
Unlike you. I do not
Have exalted ancestors.

515
00:30:59.520 --> 00:31:01.440
I make my living by trade.

516
00:31:01.600 --> 00:31:04.520
And I judge every trade
On its merits.

517
00:31:04.680 --> 00:31:06.200
You ask for ships.

518
00:31:06.360 --> 00:31:09.240
You say I shall be repaid triple.

519
00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:11.840
I do not doubt your honesty
Or your intentions.

520
00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:14.120
But before you repay your debts.

521
00:31:14.280 --> 00:31:16.560
You must seize the seven kingdoms.

522
00:31:16.720 --> 00:31:19.120
-Do you have an army?
-Not yet.

523
00:31:19.280 --> 00:31:20.600
You do not have an army.

524
00:31:20.760 --> 00:31:22.640
Do you have powerful
Allies in Westeros?

525
00:31:22.800 --> 00:31:24.720
There are many there
That support my claim.

526
00:31:24.880 --> 00:31:27.000
When were you there last?

527
00:31:27.160 --> 00:31:28.720
I left when I was a baby.

528
00:31:28.880 --> 00:31:31.480
So. in truth. you have no allies.

529
00:31:31.640 --> 00:31:35.720
The people will rise
To fight for their rightful
Queen when I return.

530
00:31:35.880 --> 00:31:37.480
Ah.

531
00:31:37.640 --> 00:31:39.280
Forgive me. little princess.

532
00:31:39.440 --> 00:31:42.440
But I cannot make an investment
Based on wishes and dreams.

533
00:31:42.600 --> 00:31:44.040
Now if you'll pardon me.

534
00:31:44.200 --> 00:31:46.680
Do you know illyrio mopatis.
Magister of pentos?

535
00:31:46.840 --> 00:31:49.240
Yes. we've met. A shrewd man.

536
00:31:49.400 --> 00:31:52.680
For my wedding he gave me
Three petrified dragon eggs.

537
00:31:52.840 --> 00:31:55.360
He believed... the world believed...

538
00:31:55.520 --> 00:31:57.120
That the ages
Had turned them to stone.

539
00:31:57.280 --> 00:32:00.320
How many centuries has it been
Since dragons roamed the skies?

540
00:32:00.480 --> 00:32:03.200
But I dreamt that
If I carried those eggs

541
00:32:03.360 --> 00:32:05.800
Into a great fire. they would hatch.

542
00:32:05.960 --> 00:32:10.000
When I stepped into the fire.
My own people thought I was mad.

543
00:32:10.160 --> 00:32:12.120
But when the fire burned out.

544
00:32:12.280 --> 00:32:14.280
I was unhurt.

545
00:32:14.440 --> 00:32:17.000
The mother of dragons.

546
00:32:19.520 --> 00:32:21.640
Do you understand?

547
00:32:24.160 --> 00:32:26.600
I'm no ordinary woman.

548
00:32:26.760 --> 00:32:29.440
My dreams come true.

549
00:32:34.120 --> 00:32:36.200
I admire your passion.

550
00:32:38.040 --> 00:32:40.880
But in business. I trust
In logic. not passion.

551
00:32:41.040 --> 00:32:42.760
I'm sorry. little princess.

552
00:32:42.920 --> 00:32:45.000
I am not your little princess.

553
00:32:45.160 --> 00:32:47.960
I am Daenerys Stormborn
Of the blood of old Valyria

554
00:32:48.120 --> 00:32:49.760
And I will take
What is mine.

555
00:32:49.920 --> 00:32:52.880
With fire and blood.
I will take it.

556
00:32:53.040 --> 00:32:56.160
Yes. my lady. but not with my ships.

557
00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:15.920
Who taught you to read?

558
00:33:16.080 --> 00:33:18.120
My father. my lord.

559
00:33:18.280 --> 00:33:20.120
Hmm.

560
00:33:20.280 --> 00:33:22.120
I taught my son Jaime to read.

561
00:33:25.200 --> 00:33:27.000
The maester came to me one day.

562
00:33:27.160 --> 00:33:29.160
Told me he wasn't learning.

563
00:33:29.320 --> 00:33:31.800
He couldn't make sense
Of the letters.

564
00:33:31.960 --> 00:33:34.440
He reversed them in his head.

565
00:33:34.600 --> 00:33:37.200
The maester said he'd heard
Tell of this affliction

566
00:33:37.360 --> 00:33:39.160
And that we simply must accept it.

567
00:33:39.320 --> 00:33:41.240
Ha!

568
00:33:41.400 --> 00:33:44.600
After that. I sat Jaime down

569
00:33:44.760 --> 00:33:47.680
For four hours every day
Until he learned.

570
00:33:47.840 --> 00:33:52.640
He hated me for it. for a time.

571
00:33:52.800 --> 00:33:55.200
For a long time.

572
00:33:55.360 --> 00:33:56.920
But he learned.

573
00:34:01.680 --> 00:34:04.480
Where is your father? Is he alive?

574
00:34:07.440 --> 00:34:08.880
Who was he?

575
00:34:09.040 --> 00:34:11.440
A stonemason.

576
00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:13.720
A stonemason who could read?

577
00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:16.000
-Hmm.
-He taught himself.

578
00:34:16.160 --> 00:34:18.560
Quite a man.

579
00:34:19.680 --> 00:34:21.760
What killed him?

580
00:34:23.400 --> 00:34:25.360
Loyalty.

581
00:34:26.920 --> 00:34:28.880
You're a sharp
Little thing. aren't you?

582
00:34:32.440 --> 00:34:34.120
Did...

583
00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:38.280
Forgive me. my lord.
I shouldn't ask questions.

584
00:34:39.400 --> 00:34:41.520
No...

585
00:34:41.680 --> 00:34:44.360
But you've already begun.

586
00:34:44.520 --> 00:34:47.680
Did you know your father. my lord?

587
00:34:47.840 --> 00:34:49.680
I did.

588
00:34:51.160 --> 00:34:52.760
I grew up with him.

589
00:34:54.800 --> 00:34:57.400
I watched him grow old.

590
00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:02.640
He loved us.

591
00:35:02.800 --> 00:35:05.240
He was a good man.

592
00:35:05.400 --> 00:35:07.960
But a weak man.

593
00:35:08.120 --> 00:35:11.200
A weak man who nearly destroyed
Our house and name.

594
00:35:13.800 --> 00:35:15.480
I'm cold.

595
00:35:15.640 --> 00:35:18.120
I'll fetch more wood
For the fire. my lord.

596
00:35:18.280 --> 00:35:20.360
Mmm.

597
00:35:23.040 --> 00:35:25.000
( horse whinnies )

598
00:35:43.320 --> 00:35:45.760
( grunts )

599
00:35:45.920 --> 00:35:47.520
Where are you going. girl?

600
00:35:47.680 --> 00:35:50.240
The armory. my lord.

601
00:35:50.400 --> 00:35:51.840
Why?

602
00:35:52.000 --> 00:35:53.560
Lord Tywin sent me.

603
00:35:55.680 --> 00:35:57.760
What might this be?

604
00:35:57.920 --> 00:36:00.520
Lord Tywin gave it to me.

605
00:36:00.680 --> 00:36:02.560
What for?

606
00:36:02.720 --> 00:36:05.280
To take to the armory.

607
00:36:05.440 --> 00:36:07.640
Why would he do that?

608
00:36:09.800 --> 00:36:11.280
Let's go and ask him.

609
00:36:13.880 --> 00:36:15.800
Move!

610
00:36:17.520 --> 00:36:19.600
Get out of the way!

611
00:36:32.520 --> 00:36:35.360
( men chatting )

612
00:36:48.320 --> 00:36:50.120
Amory lorch.

613
00:36:50.280 --> 00:36:51.960
A girl has named a second name.

614
00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:53.520
A man will do what must be done.

615
00:36:53.680 --> 00:36:55.480
Now!

616
00:36:55.640 --> 00:36:59.320
A girl cannot tell a man
When exactly he must do a thing.

617
00:36:59.480 --> 00:37:01.360
A man cannot make a thing happen
Before its time.

618
00:37:01.520 --> 00:37:03.280
But he's going to tell Tywin.
He's getting away.

619
00:37:03.440 --> 00:37:06.040
-It has to be now.
-( sighs )

620
00:37:13.160 --> 00:37:15.080
Guard!

621
00:37:19.120 --> 00:37:21.360
( horse whinnies )

622
00:37:24.040 --> 00:37:26.080
-Your grace.
-Your grace.

623
00:37:29.920 --> 00:37:32.280
My honor. your grace.

624
00:37:32.440 --> 00:37:34.560
Your grace.

625
00:37:39.680 --> 00:37:41.880
-Your grace.
-Quent.

626
00:38:02.120 --> 00:38:03.760
Lady Talisa.

627
00:38:04.840 --> 00:38:06.240
Your grace.

628
00:38:08.120 --> 00:38:09.880
I'm not sure I'm a lady.

629
00:38:10.040 --> 00:38:11.920
Westerosi customs are still
A bit foreign to me.

630
00:38:12.080 --> 00:38:14.200
It's hard to keep
All the rules straight.

631
00:38:14.360 --> 00:38:17.240
But if I remember my lessons.

632
00:38:17.400 --> 00:38:19.680
A woman of noble birth
Is always called a lady

633
00:38:19.840 --> 00:38:22.160
Unless she's a queen or a princess.

634
00:38:22.320 --> 00:38:24.320
I could find someone who knows.

635
00:38:24.480 --> 00:38:26.800
Why are you so sure
I'm of noble birth?

636
00:38:26.960 --> 00:38:28.840
Because it's obvious.

637
00:38:29.000 --> 00:38:32.400
What if I told you my father
Sold lace on the long bridge

638
00:38:32.560 --> 00:38:35.000
And my mother. my brother.
And I lived with him above our shop?

639
00:38:36.560 --> 00:38:37.960
I'd call you a liar.

640
00:38:38.120 --> 00:38:41.040
Not very noble to accuse
A lady of dishonesty.

641
00:38:45.320 --> 00:38:46.920
I always thought
I was a brilliant liar.

642
00:38:48.040 --> 00:38:50.200
Better at amputations. I'm afraid.

643
00:38:55.280 --> 00:38:56.760
Quite a pretty spot.

644
00:38:56.920 --> 00:38:59.320
Will we be here long?

645
00:38:59.480 --> 00:39:01.960
I couldn't really discuss
Troop movements with you.

646
00:39:02.120 --> 00:39:04.400
I'm not a spy.

647
00:39:04.560 --> 00:39:07.160
Of course a spy
Would deny being a spy.

648
00:39:08.640 --> 00:39:11.040
You're right. You've found me out.

649
00:39:11.200 --> 00:39:12.720
I'm writing a letter
To the Lannisters.

650
00:39:12.880 --> 00:39:14.880
"the young wolf is on the move."

651
00:39:16.920 --> 00:39:18.480
Perhaps you'd join me...

652
00:39:20.280 --> 00:39:22.720
If you've got time.
Of course. for. well...

653
00:39:22.880 --> 00:39:24.840
Robb.

654
00:39:26.160 --> 00:39:28.080
Mother.

655
00:39:33.840 --> 00:39:36.520
Mother. this is Lady Talisa.

656
00:39:36.680 --> 00:39:38.720
She's been helping with the wounded.

657
00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:41.440
She's been very... Helpful.

658
00:39:41.600 --> 00:39:43.000
Lady Talisa.

659
00:39:43.160 --> 00:39:44.600
Lady Stark.

660
00:39:44.760 --> 00:39:46.480
Lady Talisa...?

661
00:39:46.640 --> 00:39:49.920
-Maegyr.
-Maegyr?

662
00:39:50.080 --> 00:39:52.720
Forgive me. I do not know this name.

663
00:39:52.880 --> 00:39:55.520
An uncommon name here.
An old name in Volantis.

664
00:39:56.840 --> 00:39:59.560
Excuse me. my lady. Your grace.

665
00:40:08.080 --> 00:40:09.640
I've missed you.

666
00:40:09.800 --> 00:40:12.920
Yes. you look positively forlorn.

667
00:40:13.080 --> 00:40:15.640
You surprised me. that's all.

668
00:40:15.800 --> 00:40:18.720
I didn't think I'd see you today.

669
00:40:18.880 --> 00:40:20.960
I wish that you were free
To follow your heart.

670
00:40:21.120 --> 00:40:22.440
I know.

671
00:40:22.600 --> 00:40:25.040
You have inherited your
Father's responsibilities.

672
00:40:25.200 --> 00:40:27.800
I'm afraid they come at a cost.

673
00:40:27.960 --> 00:40:30.920
-I know.
-You are promised to another...

674
00:40:31.960 --> 00:40:35.360
A debt that must be paid.

675
00:40:35.520 --> 00:40:37.680
-I haven't forgotten.
-Your grace.

676
00:40:37.840 --> 00:40:41.160
My lady. News from Winterfell.

677
00:40:41.320 --> 00:40:43.040
( wind howling )

678
00:40:53.160 --> 00:40:55.800
Your brothers desert you?

679
00:40:55.960 --> 00:40:57.960
I can tell you which way to go.

680
00:40:58.120 --> 00:41:00.600
We'll stop here.

681
00:41:00.760 --> 00:41:02.440
Too dark to go
Any farther today.

682
00:41:02.600 --> 00:41:06.720
-Here? There's no shelter here.
-There's no shelter anywhere.

683
00:41:06.880 --> 00:41:09.120
There is if you know where to look.

684
00:41:12.720 --> 00:41:14.480
The cold could kill us both.

685
00:41:14.640 --> 00:41:16.520
-If you light a fire...
-No fire.

686
00:41:16.680 --> 00:41:19.000
-But a fire is...
-No fire.

687
00:41:21.720 --> 00:41:23.680
Have it your way.

688
00:41:30.440 --> 00:41:32.840
We'll stay warmer if we stay close.

689
00:41:34.880 --> 00:41:37.080
Bet you freeze to death before I do.

690
00:41:39.120 --> 00:41:41.200
Bet your life.

691
00:42:04.920 --> 00:42:06.760
Think they're out looking for you?

692
00:42:08.320 --> 00:42:10.840
-Yes.
-Think they'll find you?

693
00:42:11.000 --> 00:42:12.920
Yes.

694
00:42:15.640 --> 00:42:17.360
You're brave.

695
00:42:18.560 --> 00:42:20.280
Stupid.

696
00:42:20.440 --> 00:42:22.080
But brave.

697
00:42:24.840 --> 00:42:27.720
We start again at first light.
Get some sleep.

698
00:42:43.280 --> 00:42:45.000
Stop moving.

699
00:42:45.160 --> 00:42:48.440
I'm just trying to get comfortable.

700
00:42:48.600 --> 00:42:50.080
Stop it!

701
00:43:02.280 --> 00:43:04.600
-You're still moving.
-Was I?

702
00:43:04.760 --> 00:43:06.920
I didn't notice that time.

703
00:43:17.840 --> 00:43:19.520
This cannot be true.

704
00:43:19.680 --> 00:43:21.120
Bolton:
We've had ravens from white harbor.

705
00:43:21.280 --> 00:43:23.200
Barrowton and the Dreadfort.

706
00:43:23.360 --> 00:43:25.080
I'm afraid it is true.

707
00:43:26.040 --> 00:43:27.840
Why? Why would Theon...

708
00:43:28.000 --> 00:43:30.240
Because the Greyjoys
Are treasonous whores.

709
00:43:30.400 --> 00:43:32.640
-My brothers?
-We've heard nothing of them.

710
00:43:32.800 --> 00:43:34.480
( sighs )

711
00:43:34.640 --> 00:43:36.640
But Rodrik Cassel is dead.

712
00:43:39.160 --> 00:43:41.160
I told you. never trust a Greyjoy!

713
00:43:44.160 --> 00:43:46.200
I must go north at once.

714
00:43:46.360 --> 00:43:48.280
There's still a war
To win. your grace.

715
00:43:48.440 --> 00:43:50.800
How can I call myself king
If I can't hold my own castle?

716
00:43:50.960 --> 00:43:53.840
-How can I ask men
To follow me if I can't...
-You are a king.

717
00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:56.600
And that means you don't have
To do everything yourself.

718
00:43:56.760 --> 00:43:58.280
Let me go and talk to Theon.

719
00:43:58.440 --> 00:44:01.160
There will be no talk.
He will die for this.

720
00:44:01.320 --> 00:44:04.280
Theon holds the castle
With a skeleton crew.

721
00:44:04.440 --> 00:44:06.640
Let me send word to
My bastard at the dreadfort.

722
00:44:06.800 --> 00:44:10.600
He can raise a few hundred men
And retake Winterfell
Before the new moon.

723
00:44:10.760 --> 00:44:13.640
We have the Lannisters on the run.

724
00:44:13.800 --> 00:44:18.240
If you march all the way
Back north now. you'll
Lose what you gained.

725
00:44:18.400 --> 00:44:21.720
My boy would be honored
To bring you prince Theon's head.

726
00:44:21.880 --> 00:44:26.080
Tell your son
Bran and Rickon's
Safety is paramount.

727
00:44:26.240 --> 00:44:28.920
And Theon... I want him
Brought to me alive.

728
00:44:30.560 --> 00:44:32.880
I want to look him
In the eye and ask him why.

729
00:44:33.040 --> 00:44:35.400
And then I'll take his head myself.

730
00:44:35.560 --> 00:44:39.080
Why on earth would I trust the word
Of a lying little savage like you?

731
00:44:39.240 --> 00:44:40.880
I'm no liar.

732
00:44:42.160 --> 00:44:43.880
All wildlings are liars and savages

733
00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:45.760
With no loyalty
To anything or anyone.

734
00:44:45.920 --> 00:44:47.880
I done what I had
To do to stay alive.

735
00:44:48.040 --> 00:44:50.720
I hate the Starks as well as you do.

736
00:44:50.880 --> 00:44:53.880
Let me serve you. my lord.

737
00:44:54.040 --> 00:44:56.640
How? And don't tell me
To put a spear in your hand.

738
00:44:56.800 --> 00:44:59.160
There are other ways
To serve. my lord.

739
00:44:59.320 --> 00:45:01.520
I'm a prince now. and you'd do well...

740
00:45:01.680 --> 00:45:04.360
There are other ways
To serve. my prince.

741
00:45:04.520 --> 00:45:06.720
( chuckles )

742
00:45:08.720 --> 00:45:10.120
Like what?

743
00:45:12.680 --> 00:45:15.320
We know things. the free people.

744
00:45:15.480 --> 00:45:17.840
You know things?

745
00:45:18.000 --> 00:45:19.760
Like what?

746
00:45:19.920 --> 00:45:21.920
How to eat dirt?
( laughs )

747
00:45:22.080 --> 00:45:24.760
( scoffs )
Other things.

748
00:45:25.880 --> 00:45:28.360
Savage things.

749
00:45:30.360 --> 00:45:32.040
Wait outside.

750
00:45:48.440 --> 00:45:50.440
I always wondered
What you had under there.

751
00:45:50.600 --> 00:45:53.400
It comes at a price.

752
00:45:53.560 --> 00:45:55.520
I'm not killing you.
That's your price.

753
00:45:55.680 --> 00:45:57.000
I already had that.

754
00:45:58.600 --> 00:46:00.040
What do you want. then.

755
00:46:00.200 --> 00:46:02.480
Other than your miserable life?

756
00:46:02.640 --> 00:46:04.560
What all free people want...

757
00:46:04.720 --> 00:46:06.560
My freedom.

758
00:46:11.360 --> 00:46:13.000
Well. you shall have it. then.

759
00:46:15.320 --> 00:46:17.680
But only if you serve me well.

760
00:46:23.560 --> 00:46:25.400
-Ow.
-Shh.

761
00:46:25.560 --> 00:46:28.200
-It's not deep.
-I thought they were
Going to kill me.

762
00:46:28.360 --> 00:46:29.840
They thought so. too.

763
00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:32.400
He hated me. the man who hit me.

764
00:46:32.560 --> 00:46:34.680
I saw it in his eyes. Hated me.

765
00:46:34.840 --> 00:46:36.640
He never met me before.

766
00:46:36.800 --> 00:46:39.400
But he wanted to hurt me.

767
00:46:39.560 --> 00:46:42.280
-Of course he did.
-Why? Why would a stranger...

768
00:46:42.440 --> 00:46:44.600
You are everything
He will never have.

769
00:46:44.760 --> 00:46:46.680
Your horse eats better
Than his children.

770
00:46:46.840 --> 00:46:49.920
It doesn't matter now. He's dead.

771
00:46:50.080 --> 00:46:52.680
I would have given them
Bread if I had it.

772
00:46:52.840 --> 00:46:55.200
I hate the king
More than any of them.

773
00:46:55.360 --> 00:46:58.160
Don't say these things.
If the wrong people hear you...

774
00:46:58.320 --> 00:47:00.440
But you're not the wrong people.

775
00:47:05.720 --> 00:47:07.840
Don't trust anybody.

776
00:47:08.000 --> 00:47:10.000
Life is safer that way.

777
00:47:37.560 --> 00:47:40.480
( murmurs )

778
00:47:49.480 --> 00:47:52.080
And where are you going?

779
00:47:53.400 --> 00:47:55.800
I have something for you
From prince Theon.

780
00:47:55.960 --> 00:47:58.520
-What?
-Me.

781
00:48:00.920 --> 00:48:03.480
He says I'm to make the rounds.

782
00:48:09.480 --> 00:48:11.760
And keep you warm.

783
00:48:16.640 --> 00:48:19.040
( groans )

784
00:48:21.920 --> 00:48:24.320
( whistles )

785
00:48:33.200 --> 00:48:35.400
( panting )

786
00:48:37.920 --> 00:48:41.120
The spice king refuses me
Because I'm a bad investment.

787
00:48:41.280 --> 00:48:44.520
The silk king won't support me
Because of his business with
The Lannisters.

788
00:48:44.680 --> 00:48:46.520
Why offend his best customer?

789
00:48:46.680 --> 00:48:49.760
And the copper king
Offers me a single ship

790
00:48:49.920 --> 00:48:52.880
On the condition that I lie
With him for a night.

791
00:48:53.040 --> 00:48:55.840
Does he think I will
Whore myself for a boat?

792
00:48:56.000 --> 00:48:59.240
When I came to this city.
I had nothing.

793
00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:01.680
Truly nothing.

794
00:49:01.840 --> 00:49:03.720
I slept by the docks.

795
00:49:03.880 --> 00:49:06.680
And when I could find
Work loading the ships. I would eat.

796
00:49:06.840 --> 00:49:09.080
If not. I dreamed of food.

797
00:49:09.240 --> 00:49:12.200
Today I am the richest man in Qarth.

798
00:49:12.360 --> 00:49:14.640
Do you think the path
From poverty to wealth

799
00:49:14.800 --> 00:49:16.720
Is always pure and honorable?

800
00:49:16.880 --> 00:49:20.200
I have done many things. khaleesi.

801
00:49:20.360 --> 00:49:22.680
That a righteous man would condemn.

802
00:49:22.840 --> 00:49:25.840
And here I am. with no regrets.

803
00:49:38.640 --> 00:49:41.920
Bar the gates. Ring the bells.

804
00:49:42.080 --> 00:49:44.640
Slowly. khaleesi.

805
00:49:44.800 --> 00:49:46.440
-( bells tolling )
-( people shouting )

806
00:49:53.720 --> 00:49:55.840
Where are they?

807
00:50:02.120 --> 00:50:04.600
Where are my dragons?!

808
00:50:10.040 --> 00:50:12.600
( dragons screeching )

809
00:50:31.560 --> 00:50:34.120
( theme music playing )
